---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const join = (path: string) => `${baseUrl.replace(/\/$/, '')}${path}`;
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="auth0-stats"
  description="Tenant-wide Auth0 health snapshot by natural-language window — daily volume, MAU, failure rate, MFA adoption, top connections."
  eyebrow="Tutorial"
  lede="After this page you will be able to pull a stakeholder-ready authentication health summary for any time window — this week, last 30 days, or a custom span — from the LINQ sandbox tenant in one command."
  breadcrumb={[
    { label: 'Home', href: join('/') },
    { label: 'Tutorials', href: join('/tutorials/') },
    { label: 'auth0-stats' },
  ]}
>
  <Callout variant="info" label="TL;DR">
    <ul>
      <li><strong>What it does:</strong> Fetches tenant-level Auth0 aggregate metrics — daily login volume, monthly active users, failure rate, MFA adoption, and top connections — for a natural-language time window.</li>
      <li><strong>When to reach for it:</strong> Any time a stakeholder asks "how is our auth health?" or "what's our MFA adoption this week?" rather than asking about a specific event or user.</li>
      <li><strong>The one command to know:</strong> <code>/auth0-stats this week</code></li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="when-to-use">When to use this skill</h2>
  <p>Use <code>auth0-stats</code> when a LINQ stakeholder or program manager asks for a tenant-level view of authentication activity on the LINQ sandbox tenant. The skill responds to phrasing such as "auth health," "login volume," "MAU," "monthly active users," "failure rate this week," "MFA adoption," and "top connections." It is the right starting point for a demo or a weekly health check — stakeholder-friendly aggregates rather than engineer-on-call triage.</p>
  <p>This skill is <em>not</em> for per-user investigation (use <code>ha-debug get-user</code> or <code>/auth0-logs</code>), specific event lookup (use <code>/auth0-logs</code>), Auth0 configuration changes, real-time alerting, destructive operations, or production-tenant queries. All five sections are read-only and sandbox-only by design.</p>

  <h2 id="prerequisites">Prerequisites</h2>
  <Callout variant="warn" label="Missing read:stats scope">
    If the script exits with <code>auth_failed</code> and the hint mentions <code>read:stats</code>, the M2M app needs that scope added. See <code>docs/developer/onboarding.md</code> for the upgrade path.
  </Callout>
  <ul>
    <li><strong><code>AUTH0_DOMAIN</code></strong>, <strong><code>AUTH0_CLIENT_ID</code></strong>, <strong><code>AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET</code></strong> — set in <code>.env</code> at the repo root. The script loads <code>.env</code> itself via the shared <code>load_dotenv</code> helper — no manual <code>source .env</code> needed.</li>
    <li><strong>Required M2M scopes:</strong> <code>read:stats</code> (for the <code>daily</code> and <code>mau</code> sections) plus <code>read:logs</code> (for <code>failures</code>, <code>mfa-adoption</code>, and <code>top-connections</code>) on the LINQ sandbox tenant.</li>
    <li><strong>First-time setup:</strong> <code>cp .env.example .env</code>, fill in credentials. See <code>docs/developer/onboarding.md</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="walkthrough">Walkthrough</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <p><strong>Invoke:</strong></p>
      <pre><code>/auth0-stats this week</code></pre>
      <p>The skill maps "this week" to <code>--window this-week</code>, runs all five sections by default (daily volume, MAU, failures, MFA adoption, and top connections), and returns a structured narrative — no pre-flight confirmation because the skill is read-only.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p><strong>Read the response.</strong> Focus first on <code>failure_rate</code> (failures ÷ total — flagged if above 5%), then <code>mfa_adoption_rate</code> (flagged if below 50% on a tenant that should require MFA), then the <code>top_connections</code> list to understand which auth providers are active.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p><strong>Narrow with <code>--include</code> / <code>--exclude</code>.</strong> If you only need the failure rate and MFA numbers, pass <code>--include failures,mfa-adoption</code>. To drop the MAU section from a quick daily check, pass <code>--exclude mau</code>. Available section names are <code>daily</code>, <code>mau</code>, <code>failures</code>, <code>mfa-adoption</code>, and <code>top-connections</code>.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p><strong>Common follow-ups.</strong> If the failure rate is elevated, hand off to <a href={join('/tutorials/auth0-logs/')}>auth0-logs</a> — for example, <code>/auth0-logs type:fp</code> — to drill into the specific wrong-password events driving the spike.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <Callout variant="self-check" label="Did it work?">
    <ul>
      <li>The response opens with "Tenant auth health for …" and a window description — not raw JSON.</li>
      <li>You see one bullet each for daily volume, MAU, failure rate, MFA adoption, and top connections (unless you filtered with <code>--include</code> or <code>--exclude</code>).</li>
      <li>If the sandbox tenant had low traffic in the window, the skill notes that rather than implying a problem.</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="output-shape">Output shape</h2>
  <p>The script writes a JSON envelope to stdout with one key per requested section. The envelope also carries <code>window</code>, <code>generated_at</code>, and a <code>capped</code> flag on any section that hit Auth0's 1,000-result ceiling. See <a href="https://github.com/shannoncarver/hackathon-may-2026/blob/main/.claude/skills/auth0-stats/SKILL.md"><code>.claude/skills/auth0-stats/SKILL.md</code></a> for the full schema.</p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  "window": "this-week",
  "generated_at": "2026-05-06T12:00:00Z",
  "daily": { "logins_per_day": [...], "capped": false },
  "mau": { "active_users": 42 },
  "failures": { "total": 18, "failure_rate": 0.04, "capped": false },
  "mfa_adoption": { "mfa_rate": 0.71 },
  "top_connections": [{ "name": "Username-Password-Authentication", "count": 390 }]
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong><code>missing_env</code>:</strong> <code>.env</code> is not populated. Run <code>cp .env.example .env</code> and fill in the Auth0 credentials. See <code>docs/developer/onboarding.md</code>.</li>
    <li><strong><code>auth_failed</code>:</strong> The M2M token request failed. Read the <code>hint</code> field from the stderr JSON — if it names the token endpoint, your client ID or secret is wrong; if it mentions <code>read:stats</code>, the M2M app needs that scope; if it mentions the cache, delete <code>.auth0-token.json</code> and retry.</li>
    <li><strong><code>bad_window</code> (exit 7):</strong> The <code>--window</code> value was not recognized. Supported values are <code>today</code>, <code>yesterday</code>, <code>this-week</code>, <code>24h</code>, <code>7d</code>, <code>30d</code>, <code>90d</code>, and any <code>NNd</code> form.</li>
    <li><strong><code>rate_limited</code>:</strong> The sandbox tenant rate limit was hit. Wait a moment and retry, or narrow the window.</li>
    <li><strong><code>api_error</code>:</strong> An unexpected API error occurred. The skill surfaces the message verbatim — check the Auth0 status page if it persists.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="where-this-fits">Where this fits</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Pillar:</strong> <a href={join('/how-it-works/')}>Skills management</a></li>
    <li><strong>Decision:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/shannoncarver/hackathon-may-2026/blob/main/docs/decisions/0019-auth0-stats-skill.md">0019 — Auth0 stats skill</a> (see also <a href="https://github.com/shannoncarver/hackathon-may-2026/blob/main/docs/decisions/0014-auth0-logs-skill.md">0014</a> for the sibling hybrid-approach decision)</li>
    <li><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/shannoncarver/hackathon-may-2026/blob/main/.claude/skills/auth0-stats/SKILL.md"><code>.claude/skills/auth0-stats/SKILL.md</code></a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="next">Try the next skill</h2>
  <p>When the health snapshot surfaces an elevated failure rate or an unusual event pattern, move to <a href={join('/tutorials/auth0-logs/')}>auth0-logs</a> to drill into the specific events behind the numbers — that is the natural health-to-incident handoff.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
